WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:17.790
Captives

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.130
Okay, all set over here.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.670
How're things on your end?

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.960
Fine. All set over here.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.210
Coconna, wake up! We've got work to do!

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.630
Get the food stores together!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.670
Right...

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:43.080
Hey, Pops. You think we'll see
Zophie's guys again?

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.130
Dunno, but she's through causing us trouble.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:50.380
Those well-chosen words of yours
took the wind out of her sails.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.170
I wasn't even thinking straight.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.540
I wonder if she'd go after Chirico
if we ran into her again?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.330
Quit worrying about it.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.000
We've gotta get all this stuff done right now.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.170
Leave Chirico for the Phantom Lady
to worry about.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.170
You've already lost that battle!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.880
I know that!

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.710
You know, you never know when to shut up!

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.040
'Cuz certain people never understand
unless I say it!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.170
We're a pretty large family at this point,
so get to loading the supplies!

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.750
And be sure to take lots of booze, okay?!

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.210
What do you think?

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.750
We're going...

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.880
...camping or something...?!

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.130
I'm just...

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.420
...thinking about our own good!

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.960
Would you cut it out and
put your masks on before you both die?

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.580
Now, can we get back to work?

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.750
Right.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.750
Oh, getting it to work?

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.710
Yeah.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.750
Chirico without an AT is like a fish without water.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.040
It'll give us a better chance
when we scram out of here.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.420
No kidding.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.920
Chirico in an AT is worth a hundred guys.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.500
I'm not leaving here.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.250
What?!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:03:59.960
You're not?!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.170
Come on, a major Balarant force
is on its way here!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.630
I know.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.210
Wait, what'll you do if you stay behind here?

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.380
Keep working on this AT.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.040
You're hopeless, you know that?!

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.830
Don't you think about anything else
but getting revenge?!

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.790
You're going to stay behind and fight?

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.920
They're after Fyana.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.250
If you stay with us, you'll be risking your lives.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.630
Now what are you talking about?

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.580
You're really dense, you know that?!

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.790
Why do you always have to find
the dangerous bridges to cross?

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.920
Why don't you think about your future for once?!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.080
Come with us.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.880
Damn it, Chirico, cut it out!

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.880
After all the worrying we've done about you...

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.130
Are you listening to me?!

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.130
I said stop this!

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:57.250
You always walk around looking like
the world's about to end!

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.080
Lighten up for a change,
you god damned stubborn idiot!

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.000
You're an animal, you know that?!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.250
You should give a damn about
your own life for a change!

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.830
Come on, Pops! Let's go!

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:15.210
You're willing to risk your life for the PS girl?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.960
Hm? PS?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.830
You mean Miss Phantom?

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.540
She's really weak.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.710
That's why he came here. For jijirium.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.500
I'm right, aren't I? Aren't I, Chirico?

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.330
Forget it! Forget it!

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.250
We're running away and that's that!

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.880
Vanilla, have your brains rotted out completely?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.630
Yep. Rotted. Totally.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.460
With mold and everything. Look!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.500
Now, look...

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:53.670
When you think about it,
it's a miracle we've come this far.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.630
I don't think we should go and
abandon Chirico just now.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.040
And you're saying my brains are rotten?!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.330
Yeah, well...

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.790
So, we share the same fate, huh?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.330
Well, they're not gonna kill us
with missiles right off the bat.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.170
The Balarant are after
the Phantom Lady, after all.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.750
Don't underestimate them. Get out of here!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.210
Oh, and what's your problem, now?!

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:20.210
When you're on a snake path,
look for a snake to be your guide.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.000
Okay, let's get ready for battle. C'mon!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Right!

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.540
What?!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.380
Run that by me again!

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:34.710
I said drop what you're doing.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.540
Wake up and forget about loading the food!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:38.960
What's with you?!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.420
First it's get the food
and now it's don't get the food!

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.960
Would you make up your mind?!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.540
There's nothing I can do about it.
Chirico isn't coming.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.330
Chirico?

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.830
Yeah, we can't just leave him behind.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.630
Whoa, Coconna!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.830
What are you, stupid?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.170
Didn't the last time teach you a lesson?

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.130
Every time... you worry about Chirico...

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.920
...you end up risking your lives.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.830
Two stupid go-for-nothings, that's us.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:08.710
Right, Pops?

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.580
Yeah, exactly.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.290
But that's what I love about you guys.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.960
Figured you'd feel that way.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.420
What's the situation with the fugitve PS?

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:28.540
Our scout ship reports it's still
at the supply station.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:30.170
Any sign of the Teltain?

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.130
Not as yet.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:36.040
We've lost track of the remaining
pursuit team they sent after the PS.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.460
They may have been destroyed in our attack.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.670
No, they'll be showing up.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.420
They won't let the PS go.
They have their own PS, too.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.040
What? A PS that's trying to kill the other PS?!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.040
You've heard how well
that ship was fighting them.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.630
How could they hold their own
without their own PS?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.670
Things should get very interesting, soon.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.420
You should eat a little.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.420
I don't want any. You eat it.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.540
Chirico, you're staying behind here?

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.830
For my sake?

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.210
I'm all right now.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.670
You haven't recovered yet.

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.420
There's jijirium here. You don't have to-

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:40.000
I've made up my mind. You don't have to worry.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.170
Chirico...

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.330
AT team, stand by to drop!

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.460
Capture all the fugitives!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.290
All ships, commence cover fire!

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.880
All right, here they come!

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.920
Little more... Little more...

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:43.670
Gotcha!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.330
Pops, ammo!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.790
Right, coming!

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.710
Holy...!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.630
Great! Come on, straighten out!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.000
No time for that!

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:49.750
Here they come!

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.170
Piece of cake!

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.670
We're not doing enough damage!

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.830
Wanna steal an AT, Vanilla?

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.170
Hey, good idea!

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:09.960
We could show them a thing or two, huh?

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:10.790
All right?

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:11.630
Let's go!

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.130
Whoa!

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.830
Hey, Pops. Why don't we take this one?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:27.080
Sure, go on. Take it.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.420
Whoa! Whoa!

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.170
We surrender! We surrender!

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:48.710
It's dangerous here. Follow me!

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:50.830
I can fight!

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.920
Forget it. Come on!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.130
Any resistance and your two friends die!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:19.880
Vanilla!

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.790
Sorry about this! We sorta got captured.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.630
We've brought Chirico, sir.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.500
Leave us.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:06.330
Yes, sir!

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.920
I haven't seen you since Kummen, Chirico.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.710
You look shocked.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:19.250
Back then, I was a Melkian
Intelligence Officer for Gilgamesh.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.580
Now I'm a Balarant commander.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.580
Do you find that dishonorable?

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.040
Who are you, really?

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.920
Hmm... A man from the kingdom of Heaven.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:35.000
Think of me like that.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.670
You were never just after the Prototype, were you?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:44.830
Why me?

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:46.460
You've piqued my interest.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.250
I doubt that's the only reason.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.080
My desires run very deep, Chirico.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:55.750
My three friends aren't involved in this.

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:57.170
Let them go.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:58.630
On one condition.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.330
Condition?

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:03.420
That you and Ypsilon have a showdown.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.710
A showdown with Ypsilon?

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.830
I am most interested in seeing that.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:10.750
Guards!

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:13.960
Take him.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:14.880
Yes, sir!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:15.880
Walk!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.580
I expect an answer later, Chirico.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.130
Go on. Inside!

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:27.080
Chirico!

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.420
Glad to see you're back.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.710
We thought they'd killed you or something.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:46.210
Chirico, I know how we can get out of here!

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:47.210
Pops!

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.750
They've got ATs in the service bay.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.080
Just grab one and raise some hell.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.080
While you're doing that,
we'll steal a space ship and escape.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.960
What, don't you want to escape?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.540
If we don't do something quick

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:16.000
we don't know what'll happen
to the Phantom Lady!

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.630
According to the scout ship that's just returned,

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:59.210
the Balarant have taken
the supply station on Sunsa.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:03.670
So, you're saying Chirico and Proto One
are in the Balarant's hands?

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:06.500
Yes, sir, although our reports
in that area are incomplete.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.920
I'm worried about Ypsilon's condition.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.960
He never showed up in
the scout ship's visual range.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:14.290
Ypsilon is headed for that supply station.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.790
I agree. He's after Chirico, after all.

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:19.290
Any contact with Ypsilon?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.290
Nothing from him, sir.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:26.630
At this rate, the Balarant mobile forces
can make things very bad for us.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.580
There's even the risk that
they'll capture Ypsilon as well.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.960
Is there any way we can recover him?

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:35.960
Only if we send the scout ship out again.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.460
Into the middle of the Balarant's defenses?!

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:39.250
We'll have to risk it!

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:41.250
Ypsilon may object to your recovery efforts.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.210
What are you saying? He's just a weapon.

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:47.250
He can't disobey orders. Or can he?!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.630
An excellent question,
given his current condition.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.750
One which has piqued
our scientific curiosity. Right?

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:55.420
Right.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.880
You seem to be taking this situation very calmly.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.750
So, have you made your escape plans yet?

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.580
Shut up!

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.290
Please, no need to get angry.

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:21.130
Chirico, what is your answer?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.420
Ypsilon will come, just as you expect.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.330
Yes, as long as you and the Prototype are here.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:32.170
So, I suppose you have some conditions.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.710
If I ask that my friends be protected...

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:39.130
We'll show them every courtesy.
Even give them a small ship.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:41.380
Chirico, don't let him fool you!

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:42.750
Right! It's a trap!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:46.460
Chirico, I dunno what he's after, but make sure
any conditions include Miss Phantom!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.710
Don't push your luck!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.290
Chirico, I give you my word.

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.960
Take these three to the troop area.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:53.830
Yes, sir!

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.040
What the...?!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:56.080
What are you doing?!

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.080
Lemme go!

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:59.670
Hands off, you perverts!

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:02.500
Chirico!

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.130
Capture Proto One. Kill everyone else here!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:26.380
Roger!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:46.170
Enemy attack!

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.170
So, Ypsilon... You've come.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.880
Scramble AT teams!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.880
Send Chirico out as well!

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:03.210
All ships, lift off and hold at
altitude point X-231. Return fire!

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:52.210
How do you feel?

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.880
Ypsilon's come, hasn't he?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.750
Yes. Come with me.

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.250
Chirico, where are you?!

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.830
Chirico, where are you?! Come out and face me!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:40.130
Ypsilon!

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:48.380
There you are, Chirico...

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.210
Nothing's here to get in our way.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:06.540
This time, I'll kill you!

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:23.960
Chirico...

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:36.080
His will to fight was practically a madness.

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:40.670
But, as opposed to him, my heart didn't burn.

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:44.790
The thing that drove me on...

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:48.670
was an almost pitiful craving for battle
that raged within me.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:58.830
Why? Why do they fight?

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:01.670
What drives them to aim their guns at each other?

00:23:02.580 --> 00:23:06.500
In the underground depths into which they fall,
two men will peer into each other's hearts.

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:12.540
There, in a desolate desert,
when the guns stand exhausted,

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:14.920
a lonely figure is seen.

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:18.250
Next time, "Darkness"

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:20.790
Only death will finally separate them.

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Darkness

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
